# Project Rules for AI Assistant

## Tech Stack
- Kotlin + Jetpack Compose + Material 3
- **Dagger** (NOT Hilt!) for DI with feature-scoped components
- **Room** for database with relations/joins
- **Ktor Client** (NOT Retrofit!) for networking
- Kotlinx Serialization for JSON
- kotlinx.collections.immutable

## Architecture

### Clean Architecture Layers
- `domain/` - public models, repositories, use cases
- `data/` - internal implementations, Room entities, DAOs, mappers
- `ui/` - ViewModels, Screens, Components

### Core Features Structure
```
core/core_features/
├── agent/           # AI Agents core feature
│   ├── domain/
│   │   ├── model/  # Agent, AContext, AContextOwner, Role
│   │   ├── usecase/# GetAgentContext, SaveAgentContext, ClearAgentContext, GetOrCreateAgent
│   │   ├── utils/  # StringExtensions
│   │   └── workers/# AgentTools, Workers (Simple, Step, Prompt, Team, Talk, Compare), base/
│   ├── data/       # AgentRepositoryImpl, Room entities, DAOs, mappers
│   └── di/         # AgentCoreFeatureModule
├── chat/           # Chat core feature
│   ├── domain/
│   │   ├── model/ # Chat, User, ChatMessage, etc.
│   │   ├── usecase/
│   │   └── tools/  # ChatTools, ChatToolsImpl
│   └── data/
└── llm/            # LLM core feature
    ├── domain/
    │   ├── model/
    │   └── utils/  # ModelReportBuilder
    └── data/
```

### Feature Structure
```
features/feature_name/
├── api/        # FeatureEntry (public)
└── impl/       # Implementation (internal)
    ├── di/     # FeatureComponent, FeatureDeps, FeatureModule
    └── ui/     # Screen, ViewModel
```

### Dependency Injection
- `AppComponent` (Singleton) implements all `FeatureDeps` interfaces
- Feature components depend on `FeatureDeps` interface, not AppComponent directly
- Use `@Inject` constructor injection for UseCases

## Code Patterns

### Visibility
- Data layer classes: `internal`
- Domain layer: `public`
- Mappers: `internal`

### Naming Conventions
- UseCases: `*UseCase`, `*UseCaseImpl` if needed
- Entities: `*Entity`
- DAOs: `*Dao`
- Mappers: `*Mapper`
- Constants: `*Const` object (no magic numbers)
- Tools interfaces: `*Tools` (e.g., `AgentTools`, `ChatTools`)

### Enum Mapping
```kotlin
// ALWAYS use explicit when - NEVER ordinal()
fun fromEntity(status: Int): ChatMessageStatus = when (status) {
    ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_SENDING -> ChatMessageStatus.Sending
    ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_DELIVERED -> ChatMessageStatus.Delivered
    ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_VIEWED -> ChatMessageStatus.Viewed
    else -> error("Unknown status: $status")
}
```

### Room Relations
```kotlin
// Use @Relation for loading related entities
data class ChatWithGroupAndSettings(
    @Embedded val chat: ChatEntity,
    @Relation(parentColumn = "chatGroupId", entityColumn = "id")
    val group: ChatGroupEntity?,
    @Relation(parentColumn = "id", entityColumn = "chatId")
    val settings: ChatSettingsEntity?
)
```

### JSON in Database
```kotlin
// Use @Serializable for complex objects stored as JSON
@Serializable
data class ModelSettingsEntity(
    val name: String,
    val maxTokens: Int = 0,
    // ...
)

// In mapper, use Json.encodeToString/decodeFromString
```

### Mappers (Data Layer)
```kotlin
// ALWAYS use @Inject constructor for mappers - NEVER extension functions
internal class ChatMapper @Inject constructor(
    private val groupMapper: ChatGroupMapper,
    private val settingsMapper: ChatSettingsMapper
) {
    fun toDomain(entity: ChatWithGroupAndSettings): Chat {
        val settings = entity.settings?.let { settingsMapper.toDomain(it) }
            ?: createDefaultSettings(entity.chat.id)
        
        return Chat(
            id = entity.chat.id,
            title = entity.chat.title,
            chatGroup = groupMapper.toDomain(entity.groupWithType),
            settings = settings
        )
    }

    fun toEntity(model: Chat): ChatEntity = ChatEntity(
        id = model.id,
        title = model.title,
        chatGroupId = model.chatGroup.id
    )
}

// Simple mapper without dependencies
internal class MessageMapper @Inject constructor() {
    fun toDomain(entity: MessageEntity, user: User): ChatMessage = ChatMessage(
        id = entity.id,
        chatId = entity.chatId,
        timestamp = entity.timestamp,
        user = user,
        text = entity.text,
        status = fromDbStatus(entity.status)
    )

    fun toEntity(message: ChatMessage, userId: Long): MessageEntity = MessageEntity(
        id = message.id,
        chatId = message.chatId,
        userId = userId,
        timestamp = message.timestamp,
        text = message.text,
        status = toDbStatus(message.status)
    )
    
    fun toDbStatus(status: ChatMessageStatus): Int = when (status) {
        ChatMessageStatus.Sending -> ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_SENDING
        ChatMessageStatus.Delivered -> ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_DELIVERED
        ChatMessageStatus.Viewed -> ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_VIEWED
    }
    
    fun fromDbStatus(status: Int): ChatMessageStatus = when (status) {
        ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_SENDING -> ChatMessageStatus.Sending
        ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_DELIVERED -> ChatMessageStatus.Delivered
        ChatDbConst.MESSAGE_STATUS_VIEWED -> ChatMessageStatus.Viewed
        else -> ChatMessageStatus.Sending
    }
}
```

### Tools Pattern (Domain Layer)
```kotlin
// Tools interfaces define domain operations used by Workers
interface AgentTools {
    suspend fun getOrCreateAgent(systemName: String, chatId: Long, isCommonAgent: Boolean): Agent
    suspend fun getContext(agentId: Long): AContext
    suspend fun saveContext(agentId: Long, context: AContext)
    suspend fun clearAgentContext(agentId: Long)
}

interface ChatTools {
    suspend fun createChat(chatTitle: String, groupId: Long): Long
    suspend fun getOrCreateChat(chatTitle: String, groupId: Long): Chat
    suspend fun addBotMessage(chatId: Long, message: String)
}
```

### Thread Safety
```kotlin
// Use Mutex for thread-safe operations
private val mutex = Mutex()
override suspend fun someOperation() = mutex.withLock {
    // ...
}
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. **DON'T** use Hilt annotations (`@HiltViewModel`, `@AndroidEntryPoint`)
2. **DON'T** use Retrofit - use Ktor Client
3. **DON'T** use `ordinal()` for enum mapping
4. **DON'T** put magic numbers in code - use `*Const` objects
5. **DON'T** make data layer classes public
6. **DON'T** use extension functions for mappers - use `@Inject constructor` pattern
7. **DON'T** mix Worker responsibilities - use separate Tools interfaces (AgentTools, ChatTools)

